{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And to return their silver.</b> The reason the verse did not speak in the sequence it began, ״וַיְמַלְאוּ״ etc. — it should have similarly said ״וַיָּשִׁיבוּ״, or it should have said ״לְמַלְּאוֹת אֶת״ etc. ״וּלְהָשִׁיב״. Or perhaps it is because the one doing the filling did not know about the returning of the silver, and the one trusted over his household is the one who returned it; or he gave orders that the filling be done publicly and the returning of the silver discreetly. It further intends to say that he first told them to fill their vessels with grain, and after they had filled etc., he added to say ״לְהָשִׁיב״ etc. ״וְלָתֵת לָהֶם צֵדָה״ etc., and the intention in this is that he did not wish to say everything at once, so that the eye of the one doing the filling would not be grudging about the filling."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:10.372040880Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}